  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Show that $3^{2n+1}+5^{2n+1}$ is divisible by $8$ for every natural number $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p7-q13-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "3^{2n+1}+5^{2n+1}\\equiv0\\pmod8",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p7-q13-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "5\\equiv-3\\pmod8",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "; the odd powers cancel.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Since $5\\equiv-3\\pmod8$ and $2n+1$ is odd,\n$$\\begin{align*}3^{2n+1}+5^{2n+1}&\\equiv3^{2n+1}+(-3)^{2n+1}\\pmod8\\\\3^{2n+1}+5^{2n+1}&\\equiv3^{2n+1}-3^{2n+1}\\pmod8\\\\3^{2n+1}+5^{2n+1}&\\equiv0\\pmod8.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $3^{2n+1}+5^{2n+1}$ is divisible by $8$ for every natural number $n$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
